('0d623e11-8030-5bbb-923a-a5769427e7ca', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 11, 11, 'Why is a "fiducial marker" (a fixed pin at the centre of the swing) used when timing a pendulum?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It is easiest to judge the instant the bob passes the centre, where it moves fastest', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'At the centre the bob moves fastest, so the moment it passes is sharp; at the ends it lingers, making the instant hard to judge. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: A (It is easiest to judge the instant the bob passes the centre, where it moves fastest).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('6129f348-75e6-54a2-9cd1-b90f65eb0f72', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 12, 12, 'Which instrument would best record the displacement–time graph of a vibrating loudspeaker cone at 200 Hz?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'A motion sensor or laser and an oscilloscope/data logger', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'At 200 Hz each cycle lasts 5 ms; only an electronic sensor and fast recorder can follow it. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: D (A motion sensor or laser and an oscilloscope/data logger).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('63fd64e5-23ed-546e-9502-318621aa686f', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 13, 13, 'On an oscilloscope screen, one complete cycle of a trace spans 4.0 divisions. The time base is 2.0 ms per division. Calculate the frequency of the oscillation.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '125', 'Hz', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'T = 4.0 × 2.0 = 8.0 ms = 8.0 × 10⁻³ s. f = 1/T = 1 ÷ 8.0 × 10⁻³ = 125 Hz. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: T = divisions × time base. A1: f = 125 Hz.', 2, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 380 318" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg3068895e-t fg3068895e-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg3068895e-t">Oscilloscope trace</title><desc id="fg3068895e-d">An oscilloscope trace in which one complete cycle spans 4.0 divisions; the time base is 2.0 ms per division.</desc><rect x="20" y="12" width="340" height="272" rx="6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="54" y1="12" x2="54" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="88" y1="12" x2="88" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="122" y1="12" x2="122" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="156" y1="12" x2="156" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="190" y1="12" x2="190" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="224" y1="12" x2="224" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5d