.3,175.6 342.1,171.1 343,166.6 343.9,162 344.7,157.3 345.5,152.7 346.4,148 347.2,143.3 348.1,138.7 349,134 349.8,129.4 350.6,124.9 351.5,120.4 352.4,115.9 353.2,111.6 354,107.3 354.9,103.1 355.8,99.1 356.6,95.1 357.5,91.3 358.3,87.6 359.1,84.1 360,80.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="20" y="302" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">Y-gain: 0.50 cm per division</text><text x="20" y="322" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">time-base: 5.0 ms per division</text></svg>', 'An oscilloscope trace of a vibrating plate: peak-to-peak height 5.6 divisions at 0.50 cm per division; one cycle is 3.2 divisions wide at 5.0 ms per division.'),
('fe6f2114-f7f6-5152-b017-88e9d7a3d7cb', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 25, 25, 'A mass on a spring is filmed at 30 frames per second, and its oscillation spans exactly 18 frames per cycle. A student claims the frequency is 18 Hz. What is the correct frequency?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, '1.7 Hz', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'T = 18 frames ÷ 30 frames s⁻¹ = 0.60 s, so f = 1/0.60 = 1.7 Hz. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: T = frames/frame rate. C1: f = 1/T. A1: C (1.7 Hz).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('e6c2c8a9-f895-5291-b8b5-ed629e3094a1', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 26, 26, 'Readings of time for 10 oscillations of a spring: 7.62 s, 7.58 s, 7.70 s, 7.66 s. Calculate the mean period and its absolute uncertainty (half the range of the readings divided by 10). Give the mean period.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.764', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Mean time = (7.62 + 7.58 + 7.70 + 7.66) ÷ 4 = 7.640 s, so T = 7.640 ÷ 10 = 0.764 s. Uncertainty = ½ × (7.70 − 7.58) ÷ 10 = 0.006 s. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: mean of readings. C1: divide by 10. C1: uncertainty from half-range.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('f92e8bc2-c6cb-59ec-97e2-a7244619e865', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 27, 27, 'A student wants to show that a vibrating mass moves with simple harmonic motion using a motion sensor. Which observation would support this?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The displacement–time graph is sinusoidal with a period that does not change with amplitude', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'S.h.m. gives a sinusoidal x–t graph and an amplitude-independent period. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: sinusoidal. C1: period independent of amplitude. A1: A (The displacement–time graph is sinusoidal with a period that does not change with amplitude).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('fbfa2db3-3e8b-58b1-b9f7-9b9111518e33', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 28, 28, 'A light gate records a pendulum bob of width 2.0 cm blocking the beam for 25 ms as it passes the lowest point. The pendulum''s amplitude is 8.0 cm and its period is 1.5 s. (a) Calculate the maximum speed from the light gate. (b) Compare with 2πA/T. Give the speed from (a).', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.8', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = width ÷ time = 0.020 ÷ 0.025 = 0.80 m s⁻¹. (b) 2πA/T = 2π × 0.080 ÷ 1.5 = 0.335 m s⁻¹: close, slightly larger (the bob slows a little across the beam). Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: v = d/t with SI units. C1: v_max = 2πA/T. B1: comparison. A1: v = 0.80 m s⁻¹.', 4, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="fga1b93bd1-t fga1b93bd1-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fga1b93bd1-t">Light gate at the lowest point</title><desc id="fga1b93bd1-d">A pendulum swinging with amplitude 8.0 cm; a light gate at the lowest point of the swing is blocked for 25 ms by the 2.0 cm wide bob.</desc><line x1="100" y1="40" x2="200" y2="40" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="106" y1="40" x2="98" y2="32" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="118" y1="40" x2="110" y2="32" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="130" y1="40" x2="122" y2="32" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="142" y1="40" x2="134" y2="32" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="154" y1="40" x2="146" y2="32" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="166" y1="40" x2="158" y2="32" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="178" y1="40" x2="170" y2="32" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="190" y1="40" x2="182" y2="32" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="40" x2="150" y2="250" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:4 3"/><line x1="150" y1="40" x2="191.6" y2="235.6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="191.6" cy="235.6" r="11" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="150" cy="240" r="11" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 3"/><text x="207.6" y="213.6" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">bob 2.0 cm wide</text><polygon points="150,266 156.3,263 156.3,269" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="154.9" y1="266" x2="186.7" y2="266" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="191.6,266 185.2,269 185.2,263" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="170.8" y="278" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8.0 cm</text><rect x="110" y="232" width="16" height="16" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="174" y="232" width="16" height="16" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="126" y1="240" x2="174" y2="240" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:3 2"/><text x="196" y="240" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">light gate</text></svg>', 'A pendulum swinging with amplitude 8.0 cm; a light gate at the lowest point of the swing is blocked for 25 ms by the 2.0 cm wide bob.'),
('bc032f58-3065-5a70-b83a-4bd9b101e3ac', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 29, 29, 'An oscillation on a data logger has 8 complete cycles in a 5.0 s recording window. Calculate the angular frequency.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '10.05', 'rad s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'f = 8 ÷ 5.0 = 1.6 Hz. ω = 2πf = 2π × 1.6 = 10.1 rad s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: f = N/t. C1: ω = 2πf. A1: ω = 10.1 rad s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('2e5d7981-1e26-526b-b050-d843c977a17d', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 30, 30, 'When timing pendulum oscillations, a student starts the stopwatch and says "one" as the bob passes the marker the first time. She stops after saying "twenty". How many complete oscillations has she timed?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, '19', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Counting "one" at the start means the count is one ahead: from "one" to "twenty" is 19 complete oscillations. (Start the count at zero to avoid this.). Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: first pass is zero. C1: 19 intervals. A1: D (19).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a9b86e7b-9ea8-5158-b552-c79c6b6acb25', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 31, 31, 'A vibration sensor shows a trace of period 2.5 ms. Calculate the frequency and the number of cycles in 0.20 s. Give the number of cycles.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '80', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'f = 1 ÷ 2.5 × 10⁻³ = 400 Hz. N = ft = 400 × 0.20 = 80. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: f = 1/T. C1: N = ft. A1: N = 80.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('614a01d1-fa32-59c7-a6f9-8df47b105c31', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 32, 32, 'A student times 10 oscillations of a pendulum five times and gets 14.2, 14.3, 14.1, 15.6 and 14.2 s. What should she do with the 15.6 s reading?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Treat it as anomalous: repeat that timing and leave it out of the mean if confirmed wrong', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '15.6 s is far from the other four (≈ 14.2 s), probably a miscount. It should be repeated and excluded from the mean. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: identifies anomaly. C1: repeat/exclude. C1: mean of consistent values. A1: B (Treat it as anomalous: repeat that timing and leave it out of the mean if confirmed wrong).', 4, NULL, NULL),
('db49e72d-50f8-55df-bf36-4d82c8b91010', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 33, 33, 'A student measures the period of a mass–spring system for masses 0.10, 0.20, 0.30, 0.40 kg and gets T = 0.41, 0.58, 0.71, 0.82 s. Use the 0.40 kg reading to calculate the spring constant.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '23.49', 'N m⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'T = 2π√(m/k), so k = 4π²m/T² = 4π² × 0.40 ÷ 0.82² = 23.5 N m⁻¹. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: T² = 4π²m/k. C1: rearranged. C1: substitution. A1: k = 23.5 N m⁻¹.', 4, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 410" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg4f7d5ea8-t fg4f7d5ea8-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg4f7d5ea8-t">Period against mass</title><desc id="fg4f7d5ea8-d">Table and graph of period against mass: m = 0.10, 0.20, 0.30, 0.40 kg give T = 0.41, 0.58, 0.71, 0.82 s.</desc><g transform="translate(0,0)"><rect x="137.4" y="8" width="125.1" height="140" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="137.4" y="8" width="125.1" height="28" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="171.3" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">m / kg</text><text x="233.9" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">T / s</text><line x1="205.2" y1="8" x2="205.2" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="137.4" y1="36" x2="262.6" y2="36" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:ro