('65f1bbc7-18d9-5768-820c-53a92b9e1f32', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 34, 34, 'A buoy bobs up and down on waves, rising from its lowest to its highest point in 1.8 s, through a height of 1.2 m. State the amplitude and calculate the period of its oscillation. Give the period.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3.6', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Lowest to highest is half a cycle, so T = 2 × 1.8 = 3.6 s. Amplitude = 1.2 ÷ 2 = 0.60 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: half cycle. C1: T doubled. B1: amplitude 0.60 m.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('cc6001dc-ebc2-517e-a698-6b46afafcccd', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 35, 35, 'Which change would make the timing of a pendulum period more precise?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Timing more oscillations in each measurement', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'More oscillations reduce the fractional effect of the reaction-time uncertainty. Timing at the centre (not the end) also helps. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: more oscillations. C1: reduces percentage uncertainty. A1: C (Timing more oscillations in each measurement).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('9c1629a3-c297-5589-9324-2166bf6b2ef6', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 36, 36, 'An oscilloscope time base is set at 0.20 ms per division. A sound wave trace shows 2.5 cycles across 10 divisions. Calculate the frequency.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1250', 'Hz', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Time across screen = 10 × 0.20 = 2.0 ms. T = 2.0 ÷ 2.5 = 0.80 ms. f = 1 ÷ 8.0 × 10⁻⁴ = 1250 Hz. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: total time. C1: T = time/cycles. C1: f = 1/T.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 380 318" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg35abc0aa-t fg35abc0aa-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg35abc0aa-t">Oscilloscope trace</title><desc id="fg35abc0aa-d">An oscilloscope trace showing 2.5 cycles across the 10 divisions of the screen; the time base is 0.20 ms per division.</desc><rect x="20" y="12" width="340" height="272" rx="6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="54" y1="12" x2="54" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="88" y1="12" x2="88" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="122" y1="12" x2="122" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="156" y1="12" x2="156" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="190" y1="12" x2="190" y2="284" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="224" y1="12" x2="224" y2="284" style="stroke:var(-