('10832c02-9fb6-51db-ac98-5d13af3c5fdc', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 49, 49, 'A student uses a light gate at the centre of a pendulum''s swing. The gate counts passes of the bob: 41 passes in 30.0 s, starting the clock at the first pass. (a) Calculate the number of complete oscillations. (b) Calculate the period. (c) Explain why counting passes of the centre gives two counts per oscillation. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.5', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) The bob passes the centre twice per oscillation; 41 passes starting at zero mean 40 half-oscillations = 20 oscillations. (b) T = 30.0 ÷ 20 = 1.50 s. (c) In one oscillation the bob passes through the centre once in each direction. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: 40 intervals between 41 passes. A1: 20 oscillations. C1: T = t/N. A1: T = 1.50 s. B1: two passes per cycle.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('48a0c748-356d-5465-adda-b2e390a9a1e9', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'a3159ca9-af9c-407a-9d2b-1f70f0f4bf7b', 'a-level', '18.2', '9702 coursebook 18.2 · Observing oscillations', 50, 50, 'A seismometer records an earthquake wave. On the record, 15 complete cycles span 6.0 s and the largest peak-to-peak trace is 3.6 mm. The instrument magnifies ground motion 1500 times. (a) Calculate the frequency of the ground vibration. (b) Calculate the amplitude of the ground''s motion. (c) Calculate the maximum acceleration of the ground. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.961e-4', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) f = 15 ÷ 6.0 = 2.5 Hz. (b) trace amplitude = 3.6 ÷ 2 = 1.8 mm, ground amplitude = 1.8 ÷ 1500 = 1.2 × 10⁻³ mm = 1.2 × 10⁻⁶ m. (c) a_max = (2πf)²A = (2π × 2.5)² × 1.2 × 10⁻⁶ = 2.96 × 10⁻⁴ m s⁻². Mark scheme (6 marks). A1: f. C1: half the peak-to-peak. C1: ÷ magnification. A1: A. C1: a_max = ω²A. A1: a_max = 2.96 × 10⁻⁴ m s⁻².', 6, NULL, NULL)
