('a23f89f9-ec5c-5409-89d8-c602d3629503', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', '4e983cb3-2f8d-40bb-bc3f-1575fb3c3a35', 'a-level', '18.3', '9702 coursebook 18.3 · Describing oscillations', 37, 37, 'Which pair of quantities fully specifies the size and timing of a sinusoidal oscillation relative to another of the same frequency?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Amplitude and phase difference', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'With the frequency known, the amplitude gives the size and the phase difference gives the relative timing. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: amplitude for size. C1: phase for timing. A1: A (Amplitude and phase difference).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('69351ece-3cd8-5fec-ad3e-5d619ba881dd', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', '4e983cb3-2f8d-40bb-bc3f-1575fb3c3a35', 'a-level', '18.3', '9702 coursebook 18.3 · Describing oscillations', 38, 38, 'Express a phase difference of 5π/6 rad in degrees, and as a fraction of a cycle. Give the fraction.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.4167', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '5π/6 rad × 180/π = 150°. Fraction = (5π/6) ÷ 2π = 5/12 = 0.417 of a cycle. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: conversion to degrees. C1: fraction = φ/2π. A1: fraction = 0.417.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('83822065-9ecd-586b-a7c2-39b9730b98f2', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', '4e983cb3-2f8d-40bb-bc3f-1575fb3c3a35', 'a-level', '18.3', '9702 coursebook 18.3 · Describing oscillations', 39, 39, 'Two oscillations of the same frequency are drawn on the same displacement–time axes. The peaks of B occur 2.0 ms after those of A, and the period is 8.0 ms. Which describes B?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'B lags A by π/2 rad', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'B reaches each peak later, so it lags. 2.0/8.0 = ¼ cycle = π/2 rad. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: later means lags. C1: ¼ of 2π. A1: D (B lags A by π/2 rad).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg4988d62d-t fg4988d62d-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg4988d62d-t">Two oscillations</title><desc id="fg4988d62d-d">Displacement against time for oscillations A and B of period 8.0 ms: each peak of B (dashed) comes 2.0 ms after the matching peak of A.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="68.8" y1="34" x2="68.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="113.5" y1="34" x2="113.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="158.2" y1="34" x2="158.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="203" y1="34" x2="203" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="247.8" y1="34" x2="247.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-