('3a9f79e2-19c0-5358-816a-ae724951f0fd', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', '4e983cb3-2f8d-40bb-bc3f-1575fb3c3a35', 'a-level', '18.3', '9702 coursebook 18.3 · Describing oscillations', 50, 50, 'A guitar string vibrates at 196 Hz with amplitude 1.5 mm. (a) Calculate the period. (b) Calculate the distance a point at the centre of the string travels in 2.0 s. (c) Calculate the average speed of that point. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.352', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) T = 1 ÷ 196 = 0.00510 s. (b) Distance per cycle = 4A = 6.0 mm. Cycles in 2.0 s = 196 × 2.0 = 392. Distance = 392 × 0.0060 = 2.35 m. (c) average speed = 2.352 ÷ 2.0 = 1.18 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (6 marks). A1: T. B1: 4A per cycle. C1: number of cycles. A1: distance. B1: average speed. A1: distance = 2.35 m.', 6, NULL, NULL)
