('4fc5933f-28a9-5055-9f89-a984e2874072', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 16, 16, 'In s.h.m., what is the phase difference between the displacement and the acceleration?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'π rad', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = −ω²x: the acceleration is always opposite to the displacement, so they are in antiphase. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: D (π rad).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('e613a78a-54fc-599f-ad47-0aa01466a8d5', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 17, 17, 'What does the area under a velocity–time graph of s.h.m. between t = 0 and a quarter period (starting from equilibrium) represent?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The amplitude', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Area under v–t is displacement; from equilibrium to the extreme, the displacement is x₀. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: B (The amplitude).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('3846ae28-b1b1-58f2-ad49-0bdd71086d06', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 18, 18, 'A displacement–time graph of a vibrating reed shows 5 complete cycles in 0.020 s. Calculate the angular frequency.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1571', 'rad s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'f = 5 ÷ 0.020 = 250 Hz. ω = 2πf = 2π × 250 = 1570 rad s⁻¹. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: f from graph, ω = 2πf. A1: ω = 1570 rad s⁻¹.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('c5186bd9-ba39-59ef-9367-44e1810e48bf', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 19, 19, 'Where does the velocity–time graph of s.h.m. have its maximum values?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Where the displacement is zero', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Speed is greatest passing through equilibrium (x = 0). Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: C (Where the displacement is zero).', 1, NULL, NULL),
