('05e00ecb-65e2-5003-9528-ac30625843d5', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 32, 32, 'For s.h.m., which graph would be a straight line?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Acceleration against displacement', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = −ω²x: a straight line through the origin with negative gradient. The others are sinusoidal, elliptical and parabolic. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: a = −ω²x. C1: linear. A1: D (Acceleration against displacement).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('f9c48670-02d9-51f8-ba82-7cdc36a38a04', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 33, 33, 'From a displacement–time graph, a student reads the period as 0.84 s and the amplitude as 2.6 cm. Calculate the maximum acceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.455', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'ω = 2π ÷ 0.84 = 7.48 rad s⁻¹. a_max = ω²x₀ = (7.48)² × 0.026 = 1.45 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: ω = 2π/T. C1: a_max = ω²x₀. A1: a_max = 1.45 m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('29ff52d5-d4d1-5951-9cb3-1a473710688e', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 34, 34, 'Two graphs show the same s.h.m.: an x–t graph and a v–t graph. At the instant the x–t graph has its steepest positive gradient, what does the v–t graph show?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Its maximum positive value', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The gradient of x–t is v, so the steepest positive gradient is where v is maximum and positive (at x = 0). Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: gradient of x–t = v. C1: steepest = maximum v. C1: positive. A1: B (Its maximum positive value).', 4, NULL, NULL),
('5b0285dc-f767-5cfb-896f-baef810a3557', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 35, 35, 'A velocity–time graph of s.h.m. is v = 0.15 cos(10t) m s⁻¹. Calculate the area under the graph from t = 0 to t = π/20 s (a quarter period).', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.015', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The area is the displacement from equilibrium to the extreme: the amplitude, x₀ = v_max/ω = 0.15 ÷ 10 = 0.015 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). B1: area = displacement. C1: x₀ = v_max/ω. A1: area = 0.015 m.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg002d5d78-t fg002d5d78-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg002d5d78-t">v = 0.15 cos(10t)</title><desc id="fg002d5d78-d">Graph of v = 0.15 cos(10t) m s⁻¹ against time; the shaded area runs from t = 0 to π/20 s (a quarter period).</desc><line x1="46.5" y1="34" x2="46.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="99.7" y1="34" x2="99.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="153" y1="34" x2="153" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="206.3" y1="34" x2="206.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="259.5" y1="34" x2="259.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="312.8" y1="34" x2="312.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36