('0de023e5-57ab-5026-bfb7-3c15b01cc530', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 40, 40, 'A graph of acceleration a against displacement x for an oscillator is a straight line from (−0.030 m, +2.7 m s⁻²) to (+0.030 m, −2.7 m s⁻²). Calculate the period and maximum speed. Give the maximum speed.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.2846', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'ω² = 2.7 ÷ 0.030 = 90 s⁻², ω = 9.49 rad s⁻¹, T = 2π/ω = 0.662 s. v_max = ωx₀ = 9.49 × 0.030 = 0.285 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: gradient = −ω². C1: ω. C1: v_max = ωx₀. A1: v_max = 0.285 m s⁻¹.', 4, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg78720fc7-t fg78720fc7-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg78720fc7-t">Acceleration against displacement</title><desc id="fg78720fc7-d">Graph of acceleration against displacement: a straight line from (−0.030 m, +2.7 m s⁻²) to (+0.030 m, −2.7 m s⁻²) through the origin.</desc><line x1="82.5" y1="34" x2="82.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="210.9" y1="34" x2="210.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="339.2" y1="34" x2="339.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="39.8" y1="225.8" x2="382" y2="225.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="39.8" y1="138" x2="382" y2="138" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="39.8" y1="50.2" x2="382" y2="50.2" style