('9b086fe2-7daa-5433-ac9d-c413f313911b', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 43, 43, 'A mass oscillates with x = 0.060 cos(4πt) m. (a) State the amplitude and period. (b) Write expressions for v and a as functions of t. (c) Calculate the velocity at t = 0.10 s, including its sign. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '-0.7171', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, true, NULL, '(a) x₀ = 0.060 m; ω = 4π rad s⁻¹, T = 2π/ω = 0.50 s. (b) v = −0.060 × 4π sin(4πt), a = −0.060 × (4π)² cos(4πt). (c) 4πt = 0.4π rad = 72°: v = −0.060 × 4π × sin 72° = −0.717 m s⁻¹ (moving towards −x). Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: amplitude and period. B1: v expression. B1: a expression. C1: ωt = 72°. C1: substitution. A1: v = −0.717 m s⁻¹.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgf6335a0f-t fgf6335a0f-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgf6335a0f-t">x = 0.060 cos(4πt)</title><desc id="fgf6335a0f-d">Graph of x = 0.060 cos(4πt) m from t = 0 to 1.0 s: two cycles.</desc><line x1="46.5" y1="34" x2="46.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="130.4" y1="34" x2="130.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="214.2" y1="34" x2="214.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="298.1" y1="34" x2="298.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stro