('4dbe4dad-1f72-5025-aa42-ea0ed2f6033b', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 44, 44, 'A displacement–time graph of a vibrating beam shows amplitude 1.2 mm and 6 complete cycles in 15 ms. (a) Calculate the frequency. (b) Calculate the maximum velocity. (c) Calculate the maximum acceleration and state where it occurs. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '7580', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) T = 15 ÷ 6 = 2.5 ms, f = 400 Hz. (b) v_max = ωx₀ = 2π × 400 × 1.2 × 10⁻³ = 3.02 m s⁻¹. (c) a_max = ω²x₀ = (2π × 400)² × 1.2 × 10⁻³ = 7580 m s⁻², at the extremes of the vibration. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: T and f. A1: f. A1: v_max. C1: a_max = ω²x₀. A1: a_max = 7580 m s⁻².', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgf085a337-t fgf085a337-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgf085a337-t">Vibrating beam</title><desc id="fgf085a337-d">x–t graph of a vibrating beam: amplitude 1.2 mm, 6 complete cycles in 15 ms.</desc><line x1="39.8" y1="34" x2="39.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="96.8" y1="34" x2="96.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="153.8" y1="34" x2="153.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="210.9" y1="34" x2="210.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="267.9" y1="34" x2="267.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:ro