('4cf7f470-4cf3-5a27-a690-bbe3a2777c90', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 45, 45, 'A student uses a motion sensor to obtain these readings for an oscillating glider: t/s: 0, 0.10, 0.20, 0.30, 0.40; x/cm: 0, 2.9, 4.8, 4.8, 2.9. (a) Show that the data are consistent with x = 5.0 sin(ωt) cm with ω ≈ 6.3 rad s⁻¹. (b) Calculate the period. (c) Predict x at t = 0.70 s. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '-4.755 cm', 'cm', false, NULL, true, NULL, '(a) With ω = 2π rad s⁻¹: 5.0 sin(36°) = 2.9, 5.0 sin(72°) = 4.8, 5.0 sin(108°) = 4.8, 5.0 sin(144°) = 2.9 cm — all agree. (b) T = 2π/ω = 1.0 s. (c) x = 5.0 × sin(2π × 0.70 rad) = 5.0 × sin 252° = −4.76 cm. Mark scheme (6 marks). M1: substitute at least two points. A1: consistent. A1: T = 1.0 s. C1: ωt = 252°. A1: x with sign. A1: x = −4.76 cm.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 438" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg363aca58-t fg363aca58-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg363aca58-t">Motion-sensor readings</title><desc id="fg363aca58-d">Table and graph of glider displacement against time: t = 0, 0.10, 0.20, 0.30, 0.40 s give x = 0, 2.9, 4.8, 4.8, 2.9 cm.</desc><g transform="translate(0,0)"><rect x="138.1" y="8" width="123.7" height="168" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="138.1" y="8" width="123.7" height="28" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="166.1" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">t / s</text><text x="228" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central