('c210e0e8-6d7c-5e66-b97b-3c2a304604ec', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 46, 46, 'A sketch of velocity against displacement for an s.h.m. is an ellipse. When the mass is 3.0 cm from equilibrium its speed is 0.48 m s⁻¹; the amplitude is 5.0 cm. (a) Calculate ω. (b) Calculate the maximum speed. (c) Calculate the period. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.5236', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = ω√(x₀² − x²): ω = 0.48 ÷ √(0.050² − 0.030²) = 0.48 ÷ 0.040 = 12 rad s⁻¹. (b) v_max = ωx₀ = 12 × 0.050 = 0.60 m s⁻¹. (c) T = 2π ÷ 12 = 0.524 s. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: v = ω√(x₀² − x²). A1: ω = 12 rad s⁻¹. A1: v_max. C1: T = 2π/ω. A1: T = 0.524 s.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg34c2159f-t fg34c2159f-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg34c2159f-t">Velocity against displacement</title><desc id="fg34c2159f-d">Velocity–displacement ellipse for s.h.m. of amplitude 5.0 cm; the marked point is at 3.0 cm from equilibrium with speed 0.48 m s⁻¹.</desc><line x1="85.2" y1="34" x2="85.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="136.8" y1="34" x2="136.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="214.2" y1="34" x2="214.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="291.7" y1="34" x2="291.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="343.3" y1="34" x2="343.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-widt