('f86262a7-e744-5491-9df8-697cb17a79f0', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 48, 48, 'A displacement–time graph for a mass on a spring is x = 0.050 sin(πt) m. (a) State the amplitude and period. (b) Calculate the gradient of the graph at t = 0. (c) Calculate the gradient at t = 0.50 s and explain its value. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.1571', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) x₀ = 0.050 m, ω = π rad s⁻¹ so T = 2.0 s. (b) gradient = v = ωx₀ cos ωt = π × 0.050 × cos 0 = 0.157 m s⁻¹. (c) At t = 0.50 s, ωt = 90° and cos 90° = 0: the mass is at maximum displacement, momentarily at rest. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: amplitude and T. C1: v = ωx₀ cos ωt. A1: v = 0.157 m s⁻¹. B1: zero at 0.50 s. B1: maximum displacement.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg2cc7f807-t fg2cc7f807-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg2cc7f807-t">x = 0.050 sin(πt)</title><desc id="fg2cc7f807-d">Graph of x = 0.050 sin(πt) m from t = 0 to 4.0 s: two cycles of period 2.0 s.</desc><line x1="46.5" y1="34" x2="46.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="130.4" y1="34" x2="130.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="214.2" y1="34" x2="214.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="298.1" y1="34" x2="298.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);strok