0 sin(πt) m from t = 0 to 4.0 s: two cycles of period 2.0 s.'),
('aab00cb3-e81b-5308-b173-fcf6bd9da32d', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 49, 49, 'For an s.h.m. with amplitude 4.0 cm and period 0.50 s, a student plots v against x. (a) Describe the shape of the graph. (b) State the intercepts on both axes. (c) Calculate v at x = 3.0 cm. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.3325', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) An ellipse centred on the origin. (b) x-intercepts ±4.0 cm (v = 0), v-intercepts ±ωx₀ = ±(2π ÷ 0.50) × 0.040 = ±0.503 m s⁻¹. (c) v = ω√(x₀² − x²) = (2π ÷ 0.50) × √(0.040² − 0.030²) = 0.332 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: ellipse. B1: x-intercepts. C1: v-intercepts ωx₀. C1: v = ω√(x₀² − x²). C1: ω = 2π/T. A1: v = 0.332 m s⁻¹.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('b529441a-982c-543e-b387-b73cf371841f', '70f5e4f8-856a-42b5-a2db-b89d66bae49a', 'cecb7488-b8aa-4ae3-af2a-d77c04d03414', 'a-level', '18.5', '9702 coursebook 18.5 · Representing s.h.m. graphically', 50, 50, 'An acceleration–time graph for an oscillating object is a = −2.4 cos(4.0t) m s⁻². (a) Write the corresponding equation for x. (b) Calculate the amplitude. (c) Calculate the displacement at t = 0.30 s. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.05435', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) a = −ω²x with ω = 4.0 rad s⁻¹, so x = (2.4 ÷ 16) cos(4.0t). (b) x₀ = 2.4 ÷ 4.0² = 0.15 m. (c) ωt = 1.2 rad = 68.75°: x = 0.15 × cos 68.75° = 0.0544 m. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: x = x₀ cos ωt. C1: x₀ = a_max/ω². A1: 0.15 m. C1: ωt in radians. A1: x = 0.0544 m.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgc5b2c9ae-t fgc5b2c9ae-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgc5b2c9ae-t">a = −2.4 cos(4.0t)</title><desc id="fgc5b2c9ae-d">Graph of a = −2.4 cos(4.0t) m s⁻² from t = 0 to 3.2 s.</desc><line x1="39.8" y1="34" x2="39.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="125.3" y1="34" x2="125.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="210.9" y1="34" x2="210.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="296.4" y1="34" x2="296.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="39.8" y1="221.2" x2="382" y2="221.2" style="stroke